# Declared properties over the two branches of the alpha band.
#
# Parsed by `attest.props.parse_family`, not by `rulec.parse`: this is a
# claim ABOUT several rules, not a rule, and keeping it out of the rule
# language leaves that language and its golden files untouched.
#
# The band deliberately does NOT declare `covers`. A stale alpha reading, or
# none at all, matches no branch by design, so a `covers` claim here would
# be false, and would be the wrong thing to make true.

family fixture.alpha-band
  says "the two branches of the alpha band never both apply, and a reading
        dated after the decision never changes either"
  exclusive: latest-high, latest-low
  stable-add: latest-high, latest-low for readings when taken-day > as-of-day

# Re-ingestion must not move a holder between branches. Two feeds reporting
# one reading, or the same feed read twice, give two rows with different
# fact-ids and the same value; a tie-break keyed on `fact-id !=` silences the
# branch for any such pair. Silence in a stop rule reads as permission.
family fixture.reingestion
  says "an exact duplicate of a reading already present changes no verdict"
  stable-add: latest-high, latest-low for readings when duplicate
